; ted-screenopen2-ignored (#1007): screenopen2, the reopen of the editor
; screen (options requester, label column, after a CloseEd run), does not
; look at the result of screenopen: after a failed OpenScreen it prints
; into the freed bit planes, refreshes the gadgets of the closed window
; and blits the freed character map, and its caller goes on with the
; closed window.  TED alone under inject (alerts answered): menu OPTIONS
; closes the screen and reopens it; the bit planes of that second
; OpenScreen (SIZE bytes of chip memory) are not allocated.
; Correct (the fix of the issue): the alert "Not enough memory for
; operation!" and TED ends with the return code of a failed start, -1
; (#357); the original goes on without a screen.
; @source none
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=20000-45000/chip+1 blitz2:ted
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=-1"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 0 3
wait exit
